{
 "duration": 110.106,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "If you're ever hiking alone in the woods, and realize the forest has gone completely silent... do not look into the trees. Just turn around, and walk out.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 11.72
  },
  {
   "text": "Last October, I took a solo trip deep into the mountains. I missed a turn on the ridge, and before I knew it, the sun was gone. I wasn't panicking yet. I had a flashlight, a compass, and plenty of water. I just needed to find the main trail.",
   "start": 12.4,
   "end": 29.81
  },
  {
   "text": "That's when I realized... the woods had gone dead silent. No wind. No birds. Not even the crunch of leaves under my boots sounded right.",
   "start": 30.294,
   "end": 41.52
  },
  {
   "text": "I swept my flashlight across the treeline, looking for a marker... and froze.",
   "start": 42.0,
   "end": 47.83
  },
  {
   "text": "Twenty feet ahead, half-hidden behind a massive pine, someone was standing completely still... staring right at me.",
   "start": 48.547,
   "end": 57.787
  },
  {
   "text": "I yelled out, asking if they were lost. They didn't answer. They didn't even blink when my beam hit their face. Instead, their head slowly tilted sideways \u2014 way past what a human neck could do \u2014 until their ear rested flat against their shoulder.",
   "start": 58.387,
   "end": 76.52
  },
  {
   "text": "Then, from deep in the woods behind me, I heard my own voice yell back... \"Are you lost?\"",
   "start": 77.207,
   "end": 83.66
  },
  {
   "text": "I spun around, flashing my light into the empty dark behind me. My heart was hammering against my ribs. When I whipped the beam back toward the pine tree... the figure was gone.",
   "start": 83.956,
   "end": 95.82
  },
  {
   "text": "I stood there shaking, sweeping my light in every direction. Until I felt warm breath on the back of my neck... and my own voice whispered right into my ear... \"Found you.\"",
   "start": 96.436,
   "end": 109.81
  }
 ],
